6,7,7,7,7,7]\nRow6: cols1,2,3=6\n\u2192 [7,6,6,6,7,7,7,7,7]\nRow7: all 7\nRow8: all 7\n\nCheck plus: (1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(2,3),(3,2) \u2014 plus. Good.\n\nGrid 2:\nZ tetromino: (1,1),(1,2),(2,2),(2,3).\nL tromino: (1,5),(2,5),(2,6).\nVertical3: (1,7),(2,7),(3,7)? Let's include to reinforce red.\nPlus: (5,2),(6,1),(6,2),(6,3),(7,2).\nVertical2: (5,7),(6,7).\n\nRows:\nRow0: all 7\nRow1: col1=6,col2=6,col5=6,col7=6\n\u2192 [7,6,6,7,7,6,7,6,7]\nRow2: col2=6(col3=6),col3=6,col5=6,col6=6,col7=6\n\u2192 [7,7,6,6,7,6,6,6,7]\nRow3: col7=6\n\u2192 [7,7,7,7,7,7,7,6,7]\nRow4: all7\nRow5: col2=6,col7=6\n\u2192 [7,7,6,7,7,7,7,6,7]\nRow6: col1=6,col2=6,col3=6,col7=6\n\u2192 [7,6,6,6,7,7,7,6,7]\nRow7: col2=6\n\u2192 [7,7,6,7,7,7,7,7,7]\nRow8: all7\n\nCheck Z: (1,1),(1,2),(2,2),(2,3). Orthogonally connected: (1,1)-(1,2), (1,2)-(2,2), (2,2)-(2,3). Yes size4.\n\nCheck L: (1,5)-(2,5)-(2,6). size3 non-straight\u21924.\n\nCheck vertical3 at (1,7),(2,7),(3,7) straight\u21922. But wait (2,7) is adjacent to (2,6) which is part of L! (2,6) and (2,7) are horizontally adjacent \u2192 they'd merge into one component of size 4! That's a problem. Need to separate.\n\nLet me move L or the vertical line. Put vertical3 at col 8? Grid width 9, col8. (1,8),(2,8),(3,8). And L at cols5,6. Then no adjacency. Good.\n\nBut then row2 has (2,6) from L and (2,8) vline, separated by col7 empty. Fine.\n\nUpdate Grid 2:\nRow1: col1=6,col2=6,col5=6,col8=6 \u2192 [7,6,6,7,7,6,7,7,6]\nRow2: col2=6,col3=6,col5=6,col6=6,col8=6 \u2192 [7,7,6,6,7,6,6,7,6]\nRow3: col8=6 \u2192 [7,7,7,7,7,7,7,7,6]\nRow5: col2=6,col7=6 \u2192 [7,7,6,7,7,7,7,6,7]\nRow6: col1=6,col2=6,col3=6,col7=6 \u2192 [7,6,6,6,7,7,7,6,7]\nRow7: col2=6 \u2192 [7,7,6,7,7,7,7,7,7]\n\nCheck plus: (5,2),(6,1),(6,2),(6,3),(7,2). Adjacent to vertical2 at (5,7),(6,7)? col2 vs col7, far. Good.\n\nAlso check L (1,5),(2,5),(2,6) and vertical3 col8: (2,6) and (2,8) not adjacent (col7 empty). Good.\n\nNow also check Z (1,1),(1,2),(2,2),(2,3) vs plus rows5-7 far. Good.